timestamp=2026-11-09T09:00:51.259Z level=INFO run=dc3d0a36 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Try that interpretation: per month per employee, total = sum(hours_worked * hourly_rate for each row) + sum(bonus for each row). Let’s check with the data.\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/timesheet.csv') as f:\n    ts = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nwith open('/app/dataset/employees.csv') as f:\n    emp = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nemp_by_pesel = {e['PESEL']: e for e in emp}\nfix_emp = {\n    '16102016795': '96102016751',\n    '68011910138': '68011810139',\n    '62020111425': '65020111422',\n    '84731091580': '87031491580',\n    '15720759071': '75020759171',\n}\n\n# Compute for a few rows as per this hypothesis\nt = ts[0]  # Jan Sierpień, 3h, bonus 800, rate 37\neid = fix_emp.get(t['employee_id'], t['employee_id'])\nhr = float(emp_by_pesel[eid]['hourly_rate'])\nhw = float(t['hours_worked'])\nbonus = float(t['bonus'])\n# total for this row contribution to month: hw*hr + bonus\nprint(hw*hr + bonus)  # 911\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
