timestamp=2026-11-09T09:01:08.133Z level=INFO run=dc3d0a36 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# That’s aggregated by month. But is this the \"total salary\" as defined? \n# Also compare to computing as defined: sum(hours*rate) + sum(bonus from tasks)? But we saw bonus column exists and also tasks exist. And there are mismatches between bonus column and sum of task pay_per_completion.\n# We need to read the task definition precisely. Let’s look up how bonus is defined.\n# \"total hours worked in the month × hourly rate\" - probably hourly rate from employee, applied to total hours in month? Or per row? It says \"total hours worked in the month\" - so aggregated.\n# Plus \"any bonuses earned for completed tasks in that month\" - so bonuses from tasks, aggregated over month.\n# \n# But in the timesheet, each row has performed_tasks and also has a 'bonus' column. Maybe the 'bonus' column is the bonus amount for that row’s completed tasks? Then sum of bonus over month. That matches the formula structure.\n# Also salary_amount per row — could be (hours_worked * rate for that row’s context)? Or maybe already the row’s total. But it doesn’t match if we use the employee’s rate. That’s strange. Let’s look more carefully.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
