timestamp=2026-11-09T09:01:14.559Z level=INFO run=dc3d0a36 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/timesheet.csv') as f:\n    ts = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nwith open('/app/dataset/employees.csv') as f:\n    emp = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nemp_by_pesel = {e['PESEL']: e for e in emp}\nfix_emp = {\n    '16102016795': '96102016751',\n    '68011910138': '68011810139',\n    '62020111425': '65020111422',\n    '84731091580': '87031491580',\n    '15720759071': '75020759171',\n}\n\n# Check a specific case where maybe rate is different?\n# Row 291: emp 79011320010, hours 3, bonus 800, salary_amount 1221\n# 3*37+800=911. But salary_amount is 1221, diff is 310. Is there some other factor?\n# Look at another: maybe the salary_amount is just hours * something? 1221/3 = 407. That’s not matching any rate.\n# Or maybe salary_amount includes tax, or is pre-bonus? 1221 - 800 = 421, 421/3 ~ 140.33. No obvious match.\n# Or maybe it’s the other way: base salary_amount plus bonus? 1221 + 800 = 2021. Still doesn’t fit hours*rate cleanly.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
