timestamp=2026-11-09T09:01:44.055Z level=INFO run=dc3d0a36 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Earliest date is 2025-03-04, which is a Tuesday (ISO weekday 2). \n# So the billing period starts on Tuesday (same day of week as earliest record). \n# That means each billing \"month\" period starts on Tuesday. How long is a billing month in this context? Usually \"month\" could mean calendar month — but with custom start day, sometimes it means a 4-week period or just aligned to calendar month boundaries starting from that anchor? Or does it mean we should group by calendar months but the payday is Tuesday? That’s ambiguous.\n# Another interpretation: the billing period is the period that starts on that weekday. For each \"month\" in the sense of billing cycle, the period starts on Tuesday. That could mean billing periods are 4-week blocks starting on Tuesday, and we need to assign each work entry to which billing period (month) it belongs based on that. Let us look at the data range.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
