timestamp=2026-11-09T09:02:05.294Z level=INFO run=dc3d0a36 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let’s look at how many records fall into each period with 28-day blocks starting 2025-03-04\nimport csv\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nstart = datetime(2025, 3, 4)\nwith open('/app/dataset/timesheet.csv') as f:\n    ts = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\ndef get_period(d):\n    # find which period: period is [start + k*28, start + (k+1)*28)\n    delta = (d - start).days\n    if delta < 0:\n        k = delta // 28  # floor\n    else:\n        k = delta // 28\n    p_start = start + timedelta(days=k*28)\n    return p_start\n\ncnt = Counter()\nfor t in ts:\n    try:\n        d = datetime.strptime(t['date'], '%Y-%m-%d')\n    except:\n        continue\n    cnt[get_period(d)] += 1\n\nfor k, v in sorted(cnt.items()):\n    print(k.date(), v)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
