timestamp=2026-11-09T09:05:26.884Z level=INFO run=dc3d0a36 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# That matches the first value 4330 for 02270326116 exactly. So the computation looks correct.\n# Also the bonus aggregation is based on summing task pay_per_completion from performed_tasks (correcting/ignoring invalid task ids), which matches the task definition.\n# And we fixed the obvious employee ID typos. We also excluded invalid dates? I continued on bad date parse — so those rows are excluded. That’s reasonable as “invalid data… excluded”.\n# What about rows with malformed performed_tasks like missing brackets? For example '273' had '[244, 900, 961' (missing closing bracket). But we extracted all numbers using regex — so we still got 244, 900, 961. That’s good (can reconstruct bonuses from available data). That’s a reasonable correction.\n# Also the bonus column in timesheet itself had mismatches — we didn’t use it, we used task definitions. That’s correct per the task’s definition of bonuses.\n# Another check: some task ids in performed_tasks don’t exist in tasks.csv (like 852, 294 etc.). We skipped them. That’s correct — can’t determine bonus for unknown task, so we don’t count it. That’s excluding invalid parts of data.\n# Also \"hours_worked\" values — if they’re malformed, we skipped adding them (pass). That’s reasonable.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
